[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5589532043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5589532043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5589532043,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTSl9iw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-08T17:56:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T17:56:46Z","body":"I plan to do code review and testing on this PR ASAP (hopefully within the next day or two) to help support it","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5589532043/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5596586045","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5596586045","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5596586045,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTZUgPQ","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T06:00:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T06:12:11Z","body":"@Meorge Thanks for the detailed feedback. I’ll address these points, especially moving the diagnostic item construction and related behavior into a dedicated `DiagnosticItemRow` class. I’ll also investigate the right-click/context-menu issue and make sure the tooltip lifecycle is handled correctly without changing the current UI. This is somewhat of a big refactor so I will push the fix ASAP in hopefully less than 2-3 days.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5596586045/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5597129054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5597129054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5597129054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTZ1pXg","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T06:32:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T18:59:26Z","body":"\r\n1. There is no Copy/Select All Pop up menu in the current master implementation.\r\n2. I checked the problem The right-click disappearance is not caused by the diagnostic tooltip hover handling. It is caused by the lifecycle logic in EditorHelpBitTooltip.\r\n\r\n`editor/doc/editor_help.cpp`\r\n`EditorHelpBitTooltip::_notification()`\r\ncurrently has this logic:\r\n```\r\n} else if (!Input::get_singleton()->get_mouse_button_mask().is_empty()) {\r\n\tif (!_is_mouse_inside_tooltip && !_is_shortcut_pressed) {\r\n\t\tqueue_free();\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThat means when we right-click the diagnostic text, the tooltip can receive a mouse/window transition and _is_mouse_inside_tooltip can become false. The next internal process sees the mouse button being held and calls queue_free().\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/627ccd68-f1da-46f1-b76a-7fdf8664f9d5\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5597129054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602418621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5602418621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5602418621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTe4fvQ","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:12:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T18:59:10Z","body":"During implementation, I found a few issues with the existing tooltip behavior. The diagnostic messages are distributed across multiple `RichTextLabel` instances at different levels, so the existing selection behavior could not select all **errors and warnings** as a **single block**. I therefore added handling to select and copy the selected content across the relevant diagnostic rows.\r\n\r\nI also found an issue with how mouse clicks are registered around the tooltip. When a context-menu item such as `Select All` was positioned slightly outside the tooltip bounds, the click could be interpreted as an outside click and dismiss the tooltip before the selection interaction completed. Similarly, when text was already selected, clicking outside the tooltip could cause it to be dismissed even though the user was still interacting with the selection.\r\n\r\nThis is inconsistent with the expected text-selection behavior seen in editors such as VS Code, where selecting text does not cause the UI containing the selection to immediately disappear. The tooltip therefore needs to remain available while the user is actively selecting or interacting with its text, while still being dismissed when the user performs a genuine outside click after the interaction has finished.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602418621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5613274300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5613274300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5613274300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTpPEvA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T04:41:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T04:41:07Z","body":"> The button appearing and disappearing was actually intentional because there is a separation between the warnings. Without it, the button might cause jitter when the mouse is exactly in the middle of two warnings/errors, as the Copy button would keep switching between the two. So currently, it only appears when the mouse is within the diagnostic area, not in the separation.\r\n\r\n@shiva-kar It sounds to me like you are referring to the separation between two adjacent diagnostic items, but I thought the behavior I was experiencing was more the separation between, _within a single diagnostic item_, the RichTextLabel containing the diagnostic info and the copy button.\r\n\r\n> Really love the look of the new diagnostic hover tooltips. Though, there seems to be some tweaks still needed, especially in terms of margins. (I tried to take a screenshot, but the tooltip refused to show up again.)\r\n\r\n@adamscott Thank you for the review! Did it refuse to show up at all, or was it just disappearing when you attempted the keyboard shortcut for a screenshot? If the former, that sounds to me like it might be worth investigating further 😅\r\n\r\n> Also, it may be done in a future PR, but we should also update the warnings/error summary area at the bottom of the script view.\r\n\r\nI've actually had this on my to-do list for a while! Replacing the current diagnostics list that AFAIK is just a RichTextLabel with links for adding `@warning_ignore`s with something like a Tree would look a lot nicer. If/when code actions get merged, it would also be nice to be able to directly access them from this menu with a dedicated button, in addition to the inline buttons/keyboard shortcut.\r\n\r\nThank you as well for your idea regarding how to do `handle_tooltip`. While it may be a notable change to the structure of the PR, it doesn't strike me as something that should take a ton of time to implement, and it'll eliminate this issue with the lifecycle of the passed-in components we were worried about!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5613274300/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614248597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5614248597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5614248597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTqKilQ","user":{"login":"shiva-kar","id":106133762,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlN5Ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106133762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar","html_url":"https://github.com/shiva-kar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiva-kar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T06:35:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T06:39:43Z","body":"> Though, there seems to be some tweaks still needed, especially in terms of margins. (I tried to take a screenshot, but the tooltip refused to show up again.)\r\n\r\nI’d really like to hear what kind of tweaks you think are needed for the expected behavior, especially regarding the margins. That would help me make sure I’m adjusting them in the direction you expect. Thank you for pointing this out.\r\n\r\n> I would instead suggest to continue the way `EditorHelpBitTooltip::make_tooltip()` worked initially with `const String &p_diagnostics`, but instead of passing formatted strings, it could be a `const Vector<EditorHelpBitTooltip::DiagnosticEntry> &p_diagnostics` where `EditorHelpBitTooltip::DiagnosticEntry` is a struct that would describe a diagnostic entry (i.e. type, text (could be still rich, with url support and more), start line and column, end line and column).\r\n\r\nThank you for the detailed suggestion. I think this is a much cleaner approach than having `make_tooltip()` depend on the implementation details of the diagnostic UI. I’ll rework it around a `DiagnosticEntry` structure as you suggested so the tooltip itself can handle the layout and styling consistently.\r\n\r\n> So I'm suggesting to move your diagnostic classes from the script text editor file to the editor help one.\r\n\r\nI’ll do that as well and move the diagnostic-related classes into `editor_help` so they are handled together with the tooltip implementation. Thank you for taking the time to suggest a concrete design for this. \r\n\r\n> Did it refuse to show up at all, or was it just disappearing when you attempted the keyboard shortcut for a screenshot? If the former, that sounds to me like it might be worth investigating further 😅\r\n\r\nYes, I’m also curious about this, since it didn’t happen during my testing after the right-click fix and disabling text selection. I’ll investigate it further to see if I can reproduce the issue.\r\n\r\n> It sounds to me like you are referring to the separation between two adjacent diagnostic items, but I thought the behavior I was experiencing was more the separation between, within a single diagnostic item, the RichTextLabel containing the diagnostic info and the copy button.\r\n\r\nI see what you mean now. My current fix should also handle that case, but I’ll verify it properly with the separation between the label and the Copy button.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614248597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5634757362","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5634757362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5634757362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT9uS8g","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T12:57:08Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T12:57:46Z","body":"> > Really love the look of the new diagnostic hover tooltips. Though, there seems to be some tweaks still needed, especially in terms of margins. (I tried to take a screenshot, but the tooltip refused to show up again.)\r\n> \r\n> @adamscott Thank you for the review! Did it refuse to show up at all, or was it just disappearing when you attempted the keyboard shortcut for a screenshot? If the former, that sounds to me like it might be worth investigating further 😅\r\n\r\nI found the issue. It exists on master. And it seems related to the fact that the tooltip can be closed for another reason than of a mouse exiting (or the logic is confused about the state of the mouse or something?).\r\n\r\n| Recording of master | Recording of this PR |\r\n| :---: | :---: |\r\n| [screenshot-issue-master.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8dce7e0-3338-4b39-a71d-6ffd3ffdbe25) | [screenshot-issue-pr.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/319a6db6-f2bb-41ec-86a1-59af0f66f046) |\r\n| | _I don't know why the colors are so off here. I even tried to reupload a new video, but it has the same issue._ |","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5634757362/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5636305809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#issuecomment-5636305809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123310","id":5636305809,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT_MzkQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.c